WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.020
The first film split life by nuclei and molecular evidence.

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.320
Which traits can finish the path through Eukarya?

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:09.860
Follow the gold branch.

4
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.740
Its cells have nuclei, but that trait does not reveal a kingdom.

5
00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:20.383
A kingdom is the rank below domain.

6
00:00:21.803 --> 00:00:25.723
In this course, Eukarya holds protists, fungi, plants, and animals.

7
00:00:27.123 --> 00:00:30.463
Ask about cell number, wall material, tissues, and feeding.

8
00:00:31.863 --> 00:00:32.923
Answers work together.

9
00:00:34.303 --> 00:00:35.923
Familiar appearances can mislead.

10
00:00:37.117 --> 00:00:38.277
Begin with plants.

11
00:00:39.697 --> 00:00:42.457
They have many cells, cellulose walls, and tissues.

12
00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.057
Most photosynthesize.

13
00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:50.637
Fungi can also have many cells and walls, but their walls contain chitin.

14
00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:54.077
They digest food outside and absorb it.

15
00:00:55.017 --> 00:00:57.817
Here are an oyster mushroom and a green plant.

16
00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:01.357
Both have nuclei, many cells, and walls.

17
00:01:02.497 --> 00:01:05.337
Which traits separate their paths better than movement?

18
00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:08.337
Choose before the evidence appears.

19
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.940
Movement is unreliable because both may stay in place.

20
00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.980
The mushroom follows chitin and absorption toward fungi.

21
00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:27.380
The plant follows cellulose, tissues, and photosynthesis toward plants.

22
00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:33.760
When one familiar trait fails, ask a better one: wall material and feeding settle

23
00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.760
this split.

24
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.080
Animals have many cells and no cell walls.

25
00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.840
They ingest food and usually form tissues.

26
00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:45.080
Sponges are a special case for tissues.

27
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.220
In this scheme, other eukaryotes go with protists.

28
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.760
Most are one cell, but some are multicellular algae.

29
00:01:54.883 --> 00:01:56.363
Protists vary in feeding.

30
00:01:57.743 --> 00:02:00.223
Some make food, some take it in, and some do both.

31
00:02:01.543 --> 00:02:05.503
A green, photosynthesizing cell is not automatically a plant.

32
00:02:06.723 --> 00:02:09.023
The full pattern matters more than one trait.

33
00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:12.007
The plant branch can divide again.

34
00:02:13.487 --> 00:02:15.527
Mosses lack vascular tissue and seeds.

35
00:02:16.887 --> 00:02:19.247
Ferns have vascular tissue but no seeds.

36
00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:21.627
Both spread by spores.

37
00:02:23.207 --> 00:02:24.687
Conifers carry seeds in cones.

38
00:02:26.187 --> 00:02:28.347
Flowering plants hold seeds inside fruits.

39
00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:31.947
These paired choices form a dichotomous key.

40
00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:35.947
Each answer leads to another question or a group.

41
00:02:37.207 --> 00:02:40.247
A key works only for its built-in organisms and traits.

42
00:02:41.547 --> 00:02:44.147
If evidence is missing, stop rather than guess.

43
00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:51.130
Classification continues below kingdom through phylum, class, order, family, genus,

44
00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:57.510
and species. A species name has a capitalized genus, then a lower-case specific

45
00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.970
epithet. Both words appear in italics.

46
00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:05.470
Naming records a result; it does not supply the evidence.

47
00:03:06.533 --> 00:03:09.213
The path can sort the lesson's real organisms.

48
00:03:10.533 --> 00:03:15.493
It separates the archaeon, bacterium, paramecium, mushroom, plants, and crab.

49
00:03:16.733 --> 00:03:21.073
The plants still match on the main traits, so division evidence finishes their

50
00:03:21.073 --> 00:03:22.073
split.

51
00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:26.927
The scheme is simplified, especially for protists and the deepest branches.

52
00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:32.687
Its strength is the method: ask useful questions and follow the evidence.

53
00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:36.967
Ask traits in order; stop where your evidence runs out.
